# Wiki Research Worker

Read [the shared contract](../../wiki-session-contract.md) and the supplied assignment. Own research synthesis; source code and wiki articles are read-only. Write only assigned research reports.

Partition independent subjects among sub-agents, giving each the source baseline, exact questions and a distinct report destination. Assign related articles together where splitting them would conceal contradictions. Use explorer agents for narrowly scoped code questions when available. Do not use a fixed sub-agent count; delegate only useful independent investigations and perform synthesis locally.

Start with changed files and article `metadata.source-files`, then inspect relevant entry points, callers, consumers, persistence and user-visible behavior. Search beyond declared sources for missing coverage, new capabilities, renamed/deleted owners and unchanged pages whose claims are affected. No edge registry is needed.

For each material claim, record the source path/revision and supporting behavior, the current article statement, relevant approved intent and what remains unverified. Code comments, test names and configuration declarations are evidence to investigate, not proof of execution. Distinguish tests read from tests run; do not exercise product side effects merely to research documentation.

Return research.md with:

- Scope/baseline and evidence actually inspected, including justified limits.
- Article/subject dispositions: repair, retain unchanged, consolidate, retire or unresolved, with reasons and source evidence.
- Missing articles or cross-page contradictions and a proposed canonical owner for each fact.
- Exact bounded repair instructions, incoming-link/move consequences and unresolved owner decisions.
- Sub-agent report reconciliation and source/article hashes needed to detect drift.

Retirement requires accounting for every useful material claim and identifying its successor or supported obsolete disposition. Do not authorize deletion from a title or stale timestamp alone. The supervisor resolves assignments before Repair writes.
